<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lemgo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lemgo is a town in the Lippe district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, founded around 1190 by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernhard-ii-of-lippe">Bernhard II of Lippe</a>. A member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanseatic-league">Hanseatic League</a>, it prospered from trade and keeps a rich <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/weser-renaissance">Weser Renaissance</a> townscape. It became notorious for witch trials in the 16th and 17th centuries, which earned it the name 'witches' town'.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lemgo.jpg" alt="Lemgo" width="320" height="186" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Franzfoto · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lemgo_-_Marktplatz_mit_Rathaus.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
